      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_shifted: insert_after_residue 153 -> 149 on human canonical Q99835 (paper numbering: ortholog:mouse, construct species: mouse). Paper (PMID 35353806): \"The sequence coding for the 3-HA epitope was inserted at position 153 of mouse Smo cDNA (exon 1)\". Audit note: Mouse SMO (P56726) carries 4 extra N-terminal residues relative to human in this region: mouse 144-165 ELPSRTLCQATRGPCAIVERER = human 140-161, so mouse 153 is Ala (ATRGP) and maps to human A149, not P153; the row's claim that the motif is identical at 150-155 in both species is wrong. 'Position 153' is also ambiguous (before/after; amino acid vs nucleotide), and surface display was not shown (a reviewer explicitly notes no non-permeabilized staining). Treat corrected residue 149 as provisional.] Mouse SMO position 153 falls within the conserved CRD domain. The ATRGPC motif is identical between mouse and human SMO at positions 150-155, so mouse position 153 (P) maps directly to human P153 without offset correction needed for this region. Python verification confirms human P153 is within the extracellular domain (28-231), 79 residues from TM1. The immediately following residue is C154, a disulfide cysteine in the CRD; this is a constraint concern that the downstream pipeline should evaluate, but the published mouse construct demonstrates the insertion is tolerated at this junction. Evidence is indirect (mouse ortholog). A 3-HA epitope tag was inserted at position 153 of mouse Smo cDNA (exon 1) in the PB-HA-SMO-IRES-Neo construct, creating a full-length membrane-anchored SMO with an extracellular HA tag within the CRD domain. Mouse SMO is a close ortholog of human SMO; the CRD is highly conserved. The ATRGPC motif (human 150-155) is conserved between mouse and human, placing mouse position 153 (P) at the same canonical position as human P153. This is indirect evidence for human SMO.",
      "residue_after": "T",
      "residue_before": "A",
      "residue_label": "A149",
      "residue_range": null,
